        }
      },
      "closure_evidence": {
        "closure_notes": "The x86 and ARM stubs are the gensyscalls.py templates. They do not interpret clock ids or timespec fields. __set_errno stores the positive errno and returns -1, so both architectures have the same libc return on the error path. The Linux syscall instruction is the excluded kernel boundary. Bionic's errno store and -1 return stay in this owner and are not part of that boundary. pthread_cond_timedwait's choice of CLOCK_REALTIME or CLOCK_MONOTONIC is the caller's argument, already recorded on Bionic.PthreadCondition. This source record does not review Runtime/NativeCore/agr_runtime.c.",
